            "kira_final": "All tasks have been completed successfully. Here's a summary:\n\n**Results:**\n- Posterior mean of alpha: **2.86873931077292**\n- Posterior mean of beta: **16.3363263781843**\n\n**Files created:**\n1. `/app/hierarchical_model.stan` - Stan model implementing the hierarchical Bayesian model with:\n   - y_i ~ Binomial(n_i, theta_i)\n   - theta_i ~ Beta(alpha, beta)\n   - Prior: p(alpha, beta) ∝ (alpha + beta)^(-5/2)\n\n2. `/app/analysis.R` - R script using rstan with:\n   - 4 MCMC chains\n   - 100,000 iterations per chain\n   - Random seed = 1\n\n3. `/app/posterior_alpha_mean.txt` - Contains the posterior mean of alpha\n\n4. `/app/posterior_beta_mean.txt` - Contains the posterior mean of beta\n\nThe MCMC sampling completed successfully across all 4 chains (200,000 total post-warmup samples). There were some divergent transitions (166), which is a common warning for hierarchical models with this prior structure, but the posterior means were computed from the combined samples.",
